message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "biomedical-signal-forensics-lab"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python toolkit for auditing wearable physiological signal
  pipelines. It targets four failure modes that commonly invalidate
  downstream conclusions in digital-health research: signal-quality
  thresholds that pass on real wrist PPG despite consensus rejection by
  published baselines; algorithmic-fairness disparities driven by
  device family and skin tone; confounded causal interpretations that
  reverse sign under back-door adjustment; and small but measurable
  downstream-task degradation from preprocessing choices. The toolkit
  includes a synthetic-cohort fairness audit, a real-data WESAD
  validation against three published SQI baselines (Orphanidou 2015,
  Sukor 2011, Elgendi 2016), causal sensitivity analysis (AIPW with
  E-values), and a downstream-classifier audit. Compliance with
  TRIPOD+AI and STARD 2015 is documented per-item in
  paper/checklists/.
